# Drafted by Gemini (R11 batch b5), edited. peeping_albert's first conversation.

~ start
set peeping_albert_met
Narrator: High in the dusty rafters above the sorting tables, something heavy shifts among the cobwebs. Pink, hairless human fingers curl tightly round the timber beam where claws ought to be, and a pair of jug-handle ears twitch on either side of a feathered skull.
-> menu

~ menu
* Watch the creature in the rafters -> watch_bird
* [Animal Handling DC 13] Hold out an arm and whistle softly -> check_ok | check_fail
* Step back from under the beam -> END

~ watch_bird
Narrator: The grotesque pigeon leans down into the lantern glow, its greasy feathers smelling of wet wool and attic dust. A wet, throaty coo rumbles from its crop before a splat of white lime drops onto {name}'s shoulder, folded neatly like a tiny note.
-> menu

~ check_ok
Narrator: The fleshy ears flatten against the grey plumage, and its knuckles drum a slow, knowing tap against the oak beam. It points one stubby forefinger toward the postmaster's locked drawer, then shrinks back into the shadow.
-> menu

~ check_fail
Narrator: The bird snaps its beak with a dry clack, scratches one human ear with a calloused thumb, and turns its tail to you.
-> menu
